WEBVTT

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:09.279
Hello, this is Jenna Fisher and Angela Kinsey from the Office Ladies' Podcast in Los Angeles.
大家好，我是洛杉矶办公室女士播客的珍娜·费舍尔和安吉拉·金赛。

00:00:09.279 --> 00:00:14.380
And something we love about How We Made Your Mother is the amazing community of this show.
我们喜欢《我们如何创造了你的母亲》的一点是这个节目令人惊叹的社区。

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:18.780
The fans and people that write in, we think you guys are awesome.
粉丝和写信的人，我们认为你们很棒。

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.679
And I love when Josh and Craig get philosophical.
我喜欢乔什和克雷格变得富有哲理。

00:00:22.679 --> 00:00:39.042
I mean, I love all the behind the scenes stories, but my favorite is when Josh suddenly starts quoting Einstein or some ancient philosopher, and then he and Craig basically break down the meaning of love, or the power of friendship, or forgiveness, or you name it.
我的意思是，我喜欢所有的幕后故事，但我最喜欢的是乔什突然开始引用爱因斯坦或一些古代哲学家的话，然后他和克雷格基本上分解了爱的意义，或者友谊的力量，或者宽恕，或者你能想到的。

00:00:39.042 --> 00:00:44.558
But I often find myself feeling a little lighter, a little more hopeful, after listening.
但听完之后，我常常发现自己感觉轻松了一些，更有希望了。

00:00:44.558 --> 00:00:47.719
And that's a pretty special thing to be able to do.
这是一件非常特别的事情。

00:00:47.719 --> 00:00:52.740
And that's why we're thrilled to be adding the show to our Office Ladies Network.
这就是为什么我们很高兴将该节目添加到我们的办公室女士网络中。

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.020
Welcome, guys!
欢迎，伙计们！

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:57.219
Oh, and you better have us as guests real soon.
哦，你最好尽快邀请我们成为真正的客人。

00:00:57.219 --> 00:00:57.878
Uh-huh.
嗯嗯。

00:00:57.878 --> 00:00:58.820
Get on it.
开始吧。

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.619
I'm alone.
我还是孤单一人。

00:01:00.619 --> 00:01:05.609
Be I won't be soon.
我不会很快。

00:01:05.609 --> 00:01:08.760
You're New York City.
你是纽约市。

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:11.379
When I see you.
当我看到你的时候。

00:01:11.379 --> 00:01:15.569
Please permit me to tell you everything.
请允许我告诉你一切。

00:01:15.569 --> 00:01:19.180
You're New York City.
你是纽约市。

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:20.489
Well, here we are.
好吧，我们到了。

00:01:20.489 --> 00:01:25.579
Welcome to the first episode of season two of How We Made Your Mother.
欢迎收看《我们如何成就了你的母亲》第二季第一集。

00:01:25.579 --> 00:01:27.079
I am Josh Radner.
我是乔什·拉德纳。

00:01:27.079 --> 00:01:33.579
I played Ted Mosby on the TV show called How I Met Your Mother, which ran on CBS from 2005 to 2014.
我在 2005 年至 2014 年 CBS 播出的电视节目《老爸老妈浪漫史》中扮演泰德·莫斯比。

00:01:33.579 --> 00:01:37.799
I am here with the co-creator of that show, Craig Thomas.
我和该节目的共同创作者克雷格·托马斯一起来到这里。

00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:39.640
Hello, Craig, it's great to see you.
你好，克雷格，很高兴见到你。

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:47.319
Hello, Josh, very excited to be back here with you and the fans and our new wonderful friends over at the Office Ladies Network.
你好，乔什，很高兴能回到这里与你和粉丝以及我们在办公室女士网络的新朋友们一起。

00:01:47.319 --> 00:01:52.760
Oh, well then, we sometimes call it, which is just to save us the energy of saying all those syllables.
哦，那么，我们有时会这样称呼它，这只是为了节省我们说所有这些音节的精力。

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:55.040
We don't have that kind of time.
我们没有那样的时间。

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.400
We're very busy people.
我们是非常忙碌的人。

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.239
Yeah, we got to get on with it.
是的，我们必须继续下去。

00:01:58.239 --> 00:01:59.079
Tell this story.
讲这个故事。

00:01:59.079 --> 00:02:00.000
Yeah, tell the story.
是的，讲故事。

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:00.840
How did this happen?
这是怎么发生的？

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:06.000
Well, yeah, we're delighted to be working with Jenna and Angela and their team.
嗯，是的，我们很高兴与珍娜和安吉拉以及他们的团队合作。

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:18.439
So the way this came about was, you know, we were a kind of lean and mean operation for season, me, Craig, Alec, Doug, Alex, just this very small team, and we were just doing this all on our own.
所以这一切的发生方式是，你知道，我们这个赛季的运作是一种精干和刻薄的运作，我、克雷格、亚历克、道格、亚历克斯，只是这个非常小的团队，我们只是自己做这一切。

00:02:18.439 --> 00:02:27.240
And I called Jenna Fisher, my old pal from back in the days, because we were on big hit TV shows around the same time, so we got to know each other.
我给我以前的老朋友珍娜·费舍尔打了电话，因为我们大约在同一时间上热门电视节目，所以我们互相认识了。

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:35.520
And I was reaching out, one, to ask her advice as a trailblazer in the rewatch podcast space.
作为重播播客领域的开拓者，我向她寻求建议。

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:53.719
If she had any advice for us, but also more specifically, I wanted to see if she would come on our podcast to talk about the strangeness of being a decade or so of your life, being thought of as someone you're not, being the whirlwind of being on a hit show, like all these things.
如果她对我们有什么建议，更具体地说，我想看看她是否会在我们的播客上谈论你生命中十年左右的奇怪之处，被认为不是你的人，成为热门节目的旋风，就像所有这些事情。

00:02:53.719 --> 00:02:58.819
And before we even got into it, she said, are you guys working with a podcast company?
在我们开始讨论之前，她说，你们在与播客公司合作吗？

00:02:58.819 --> 00:03:00.500
And I said, no.
我说，不。

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:07.840
And she said, well, Angela and I have started our own podcast company called Office Ladies Network.
她说，好吧，安吉拉和我创办了自己的播客公司，名为“办公室女士网络”。

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:10.659
And we would probably be delighted to have you on it.
我们可能会很高兴您的加入。

00:03:10.659 --> 00:03:14.939
She actually said we would be sight unheard podcast on the scene.
她实际上说我们将成为现场闻所未闻的播客。

00:03:14.939 --> 00:03:17.659
Like, how do you say that sounds on her?
就像，你觉得这听起来怎么样？

00:03:17.659 --> 00:03:18.659
Yeah.
是的。

00:03:18.659 --> 00:03:25.883
She she just and then her and Angela gave a couple episodes of spin and immediately called us and said, we love this.
她就这样，然后她和安吉拉做了几集旋转，并立即打电话给我们说，我们喜欢这个。

00:03:25.883 --> 00:03:30.204
We'd love to pull you under the umbrella of the office ladies network.
我们很乐意将您纳入办公室女士网络的保护之下。

00:03:30.204 --> 00:03:33.600
We'd love to cross pollinate in any ways that we could.
我们很乐意以任何可能的方式进行异花授粉。

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:35.019
And we're so delighted.
我们很高兴。

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:35.813
We're so thrilled.
我们太激动了。

00:03:35.813 --> 00:03:37.180
Craig, what do you have to add?
克雷格，你有什么要补充的吗？

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:38.177
We're so honored.
我们非常荣幸。

00:03:38.177 --> 00:03:39.234
They would ask us.
他们会问我们。

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:40.525
They're so good at it.
他们太擅长了。

00:03:40.525 --> 00:03:41.464
They're so good.
他们太好了。

00:03:41.464 --> 00:03:42.403
They're so good.
他们太好了。

00:03:42.403 --> 00:03:44.750
Jenna and Angela, they are trailblazers.
珍娜和安吉拉，他们是开拓者。

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:50.208
They kind of paved the way for like a comedy rewatch podcast like ourselves to come along to.
他们为像我们这样的喜剧重播播客铺平了道路。

00:03:50.208 --> 00:03:55.960
And so we're grateful that they kind of and took us under their wing and we're their partners now.
因此，我们很感激他们将我们置于他们的保护之下，我们现在是他们的合作伙伴。

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:56.800
Yeah, thank you guys.
是的，谢谢你们。

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:57.639
Thank you to Jenna.
谢谢你珍娜。

00:03:57.639 --> 00:03:58.479
Thank you, Angela.
谢谢你，安吉拉。

00:03:58.479 --> 00:03:59.379
We're huge fans of the office.
我们是办公室的超级粉丝。

00:03:59.379 --> 00:04:02.539
You will hear them on here and us on there.
您会在这里听到他们的声音，在那里听到我们的声音。

00:04:02.539 --> 00:04:04.939
We really will kind of cross pollinate.
我们真的会进行异花授粉。

00:04:04.939 --> 00:04:05.780
It's going to be great.
会很棒的。

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:06.620
We're very grateful.
我们非常感激。

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:14.219
I mean, it's kind of cool that it's when we were growing up, like, crossover episodes were, you know, like, Laverne and Shirley would show up on Happy Days, right?
我的意思是，在我们成长的过程中，这很酷，就像交叉剧集，你知道，就像拉弗恩和雪莉会出现在快乐时光，对吧？

00:04:14.219 --> 00:04:16.060
Yeah, it's like, it's the time on Earth.
是的，就像是地球上的时间。

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:16.899
I miss that.
我很怀念那个。

00:04:16.899 --> 00:04:17.819
I miss that so much tradition.
我非常怀念这个传统。

00:04:17.819 --> 00:04:21.019
And we didn't do that in our era.
而我们那个时代并没有这样做。

00:04:21.019 --> 00:04:22.500
So we're doing it now.
所以我们现在就这么做。

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.540
with our rewatch podcasts.
通过我们的重播播客。

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:25.579
We're doing it now.
我们现在正在做。

00:04:25.579 --> 00:04:26.420
I love it.
我喜欢它。

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:30.699
I love retroactively, we're doing it in this other medium since TV is too hard now.
我喜欢追溯，我们正在用另一种媒体来做这件事，因为现在电视太难了。

00:04:30.699 --> 00:04:33.899
It's too hard to make TV shows now, so now we'll just do it on a podcast issue.
现在制作电视节目太难了，所以现在我们就做播客问题。

00:04:33.899 --> 00:04:38.660
Yeah, so thank you to Jenna and Angela and their team over at Office Ladies Network.
是的，感谢詹娜和安吉拉以及她们在办公室女士网络的团队。

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:45.540
We're thrilled to be part of the family and we are putting a pause on the YouTube segment.
我们很高兴成为这个家庭的一员，我们将暂停 YouTube 部分。

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:49.300
Craig, and I'll just say this upfront, Craig and I are aging aggressively.
克雷格，我先说一下，克雷格和我正在迅速变老。

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:52.459
which is very aggressively each day.
每天都非常积极。

00:04:52.459 --> 00:04:53.939
I had a lot of work done over the summer.
整个夏天我做了很多工作。

00:04:53.939 --> 00:04:54.779
I don't know if you're talking about it.
我不知道你是否在谈论它。

00:04:54.779 --> 00:04:57.579
It has not settled yet.
事情还没有解决。

00:04:57.579 --> 00:05:05.579
It didn't take, we cannot, we in good contents, we cannot show you Craig Thomas' face right now until his work settles.
不需要，我们不能，我们内容很好，在克雷格·托马斯的工作解决之前，我们现在不能向你展示克雷格·托马斯的脸。

00:05:05.579 --> 00:05:16.699
If you were watching the show over on YouTube, thank you, we loved having you go over there and we're still gonna have some video components to the show, but we're not gonna be on YouTube every week.
如果您在 YouTube 上观看该节目，谢谢您，我们很高兴您能去那里，我们仍然会为该节目提供一些视频组件，但我们不会每周都在 YouTube 上观看。

00:05:16.699 --> 00:05:20.399
Yeah, you'll see fun videos on our socials but it won't be the full episode on YouTube.
是的，您会在我们的社交媒体上看到有趣的视频，但它不会是 YouTube 上的完整剧集。

00:05:20.399 --> 00:05:23.459
And you can monitor Craig's healing, which we're all looking for.
您可以监控克雷格的康复情况，这是我们都在寻找的。

00:05:23.459 --> 00:05:28.459
Yeah, no, I'll assume the bandages will come off about episode 11 or 12 that we're discussing.
是的，不，我假设绷带会在我们正在讨论的第 11 或 12 集中脱落。

00:05:28.459 --> 00:05:34.620
It's pretty hard to look at right now, I gotta be honest, it's kind of, there's like a drainage pipe going from each eye.
现在很难看，我必须说实话，有点像每只眼睛都有一根排水管。

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:36.540
Josh, I haven't had the work done yet.
乔什，我的工作还没有完成。

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:38.819
Okay, what is going on?
好吧，这是怎么回事？

00:05:38.819 --> 00:05:41.899
It's coming up, it's next week, this is horrible.
即将到来，下周，这太可怕了。

00:05:41.899 --> 00:05:42.980
Why don't we get to it, Craig?
我们为什么不开始做呢，克雷格？

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:45.459
Why don't we launch this season two?
为什么我们不推出第二季？

00:05:45.459 --> 00:05:48.300
Turning now to our trusty producer, Alec Lev.
现在转向我们值得信赖的制作人亚历克·列夫。

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:52.459
Alec, tell us the name of this episode and when it originally aired.
亚历克，请告诉我们这一集的名称以及最初播出的时间。

00:05:52.459 --> 00:05:53.620
Absolutely, and hi guys.
绝对可以，大家好。

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:54.459
Welcome back.
欢迎回来。

00:05:54.459 --> 00:05:55.300
Hi, Alec.
嗨，亚历克。

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:58.779
Exciting, and I'm very excited also about this Office Ladies Network.
令人兴奋，我对这个办公室女士网络也感到非常兴奋。

00:05:58.779 --> 00:06:06.019
Jen and Angela have already been amazing to work with, thanks to them from me also, and Colin, who is part of their team as well.
Jen 和 Angela 的合作非常愉快，我也感谢他们，也感谢他们团队的一员 Colin。

00:06:06.019 --> 00:06:08.060
The episode is called Where Were We?
这一集的名字叫《我们在哪里？》

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:14.579
It originally aired on September 18th, 2006, written by Carter Bays and Craig Thomas.
该剧最初于 2006 年 9 月 18 日播出，编剧为卡特·贝斯 (Carter Bays) 和克雷格·托马斯 (Craig Thomas)。

00:06:14.579 --> 00:06:15.420
Where were we?
我们在哪里？

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:17.540
It's a great question to ask.
这是一个很好的问题。

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:18.980
We, uh, we had a title.
我们，呃，我们有一个头衔。

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:23.339
We wrapped up a season one and, and we, I haven't seen you for years.
我们结束了第一季，而且我们已经很多年没有见到你了。

00:06:23.339 --> 00:06:27.180
And by years, I mean, like six weeks, maybe six weeks.
我的意思是，大约六周，也许六周。

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:29.259
It's been the smallest summer hiatus I've ever had.
这是我经历过的最小的暑假。

00:06:29.259 --> 00:06:30.420
It isn't brief hiatus.
这不是短暂的中断。

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:33.620
It's not like the real, the real hymnium hiatus several months.
这不像真正的、真正的赞美诗中断几个月。

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:35.500
I would, I would not see you for a while.
我愿意，有一段时间我不会见到你。

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:37.379
You would go off on crazy adventures.
你会开始疯狂的冒险。

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.939
The writers would come back way before the actors.
编剧会比演员早回来。

00:06:40.259 --> 00:06:42.220
We worked for like 16 weeks before you got there.
在你到达那里之前我们工作了大约 16 周。

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:45.620
All the actors would come in looking tan and beautiful and be like, how was your guy's summer?
所有的演员进来时都会看起来晒得黝黑，很漂亮，然后问，你的家伙夏天过得怎么样？

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:47.819
we'd be like, we're haggard and gray.
我们会这样，我们憔悴、灰白。

00:06:47.819 --> 00:06:49.579
We haven't seen the sun.
我们还没有看到太阳。

00:06:49.579 --> 00:06:51.259
Don't ask us how our summer was.
不要问我们夏天过得怎么样。

00:06:51.259 --> 00:06:55.060
But yeah, no, this was a quick turnaround.
但是，是的，不，这是一个快速的转变。

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:56.699
So it's fun to jump right back in.
所以立即跳回来很有趣。

00:06:56.699 --> 00:07:04.699
I love the meta title of where we, that was the feeling in trying to break this episode in the writer's room of like, how do we pick this up?
我喜欢《我们在哪里》的元标题，那就是在编剧的房间里试图打破这一集的感觉，比如，我们如何选择这个？

00:07:04.699 --> 00:07:09.779
And here's my first thought, Josh, when I started watching this one, which I did last night and I loved it.
这是我的第一个想法，乔什，当我开始观看这个节目时，我昨晚看了它，我很喜欢它。

00:07:09.779 --> 00:07:12.980
I hadn't seen this in years and years and years and years.
我已经很多年没有见过这个了。

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:16.379
And the pressure coming in his episode was immense.
他的这段经历所带来的压力是巨大的。

00:07:16.379 --> 00:07:29.019
We had been advised, slash scolded, to be less serialized, but in between the two season, season one and season two, we did not agree with that advice and we didn't really take it.
有人建议我们减少连载，但在第一季和第二季之间，我们不同意这个建议，也没有真正接受。

00:07:29.019 --> 00:07:38.259
But we really wanted to come in and kill it to show that we could do this kind of serialized, emotional comedy show on CBS and have it find an audience, but we weren't there yet.
但我们真的很想进来并扼杀它，以表明我们可以在哥伦比亚广播公司（CBS）上制作这种系列化的情感喜剧节目并让它找到观众，但我们还没有做到这一点。

00:07:38.259 --> 00:07:40.540
And so we really felt like we're singing for our supper.
所以我们真的感觉我们正在为我们的晚餐唱歌。

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:49.980
The thing the first thought I had was, It's so funny that we had to speak to the summer passing to still stay in season for when the TV show was airing.
我的第一个想法是，这太有趣了，我们不得不谈论夏天的过去，以便在电视节目播出时仍然保持旺季。

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:53.899
You were just talking about crossover episodes in like 70s and 80s TV.
你刚才谈论的是 70 年代和 80 年代电视中的交叉剧集。

00:07:53.899 --> 00:08:00.579
Another seemingly now vestigial thing is this idea that you have to be in the season where you're airing, right?
另一件看似现在已经退化的事情是，你必须在你正在播出的季节里，对吧？

00:08:00.579 --> 00:08:02.180
On streaming, who cares?
在流媒体上，谁在乎呢？

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:03.019
Who cares?
谁在乎？

00:08:03.019 --> 00:08:03.860
